REMARKS:
111500Z POSITION NEAR 30.9N 156.0E.
11NOV26. TYPHOON 31W (CEMPAKA), LOCATED APPROXIMATELY 360 NM
NORTH OF MINAMI TORI SHIMA, HAS TRACKED EAST-NORTHEASTWARD AT 36
KNOTS OVER THE PAST SIX HOURS. ANIMATED ENHANCED INFRARED (EIR)
IMAGERY DEPICTS TYPHOON 31W WITH A RAPIDLY DETERIORATING CONVECTIVE
STRUCTURE AS IT CONTINUES TO MERGE WITH A COLD FRONT. AN 111051Z
METOP-B ASCAT PASS REVEALED THE LOW LEVEL CIRCULATION CENTER (LLCC)
BEGINNING TO OPEN UP INTO THE BROADER TROUGHING ASSOCIATED WITH THE
FRONTAL SYSTEM. THE ASCAT ALSO SHOWS AN INCREASINGLY ASYMMETRICAL
WIND FIELD WITH ENHANCED WINDS CONFINED TO THE SOUTHERN SEMICIRCLE.
A PREVIOUS 110809Z SMOS PASS REVEALED THE SYSTEM TO HAVE 65-70 KT
WINDS NEAR THE CORE, SUPPORTING AN INITIAL INTENSITY OF 65 KTS.
ENVIRONMENTAL CONDITIONS ARE ASSESSED AS UNFAVORABLE AS VERTICAL
WIND SHEAR (VWS) HAS RISEN TO OVER 40 KTS, SEA SURFACE TEMPERATURES
ARE 25-26 C, AND DRY AIR FROM THE COLD SIDE OF THE FRONTAL SYSTEM
ENTRAINS INTO 31W. DETERMINISTIC MODEL GUIDANCE IS IN GOOD AGREEMENT
ON 31W CONTINNUING TO DISSIPATE WITHIN THE NEXT 12 HOURS WHILE
ACCELERATING NORTHEASTWARD. MODEL GUIDANCE ALSO AGREES ON STEADY
WEAKENING FOR THE NEXT 24 HOURS, HOWEVER WIND SPEEDS ARE EXPECTED TO
REMAIN  ABOVE TROPICAL STORM STRENGTH AS THE SYSTEM OPENS UP WITHIN
THE LARGER FRONTAL FEATURE. THIS IS THE FINAL WARNING ON THIS SYSTEM
BY THE JOINT TYPHOON WRNCEN PEARL HARBOR HI. THE SYSTEM WILL BE CLOSELY
MONITORED FOR SIGNS OF REGENERATION. MINIMUM CENTRAL PRESSURE AT
111200Z IS 983 MB. MAXIMUM SIGNIFICANT WAVE HEIGHT AT 111200Z IS 30
FEET.
